From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:39:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: support local private configuration overrides

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: separate local private settings from portable main config
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1007-personal-feature-disable-hosted-services-telemetry-and-promotions.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 1013-personal-feature-local-private-configuration.patch

Patch intent:
Load optional config.private.toml beside the logical main configuration,
merging TOML tables before typed defaults and environment overrides. Keep
private values out of main-file saves and configuration displays, expose
value-free override notices, and reload when either configuration changes.
Both files support symlinks, including a main file pointing into dotfiles.

Why it exists:
Users need portable configuration and local private settings without a
modular configuration system or Git integration. Private settings remain
plaintext and user-managed. Updates preserve main-file settings and unknown
keys instead of flattening effective private or environment values. Saving
a shadowed setting must not claim it became effective. Explicit session
switches remain distinct from stored default changes. The feature does not
automatically edit private files or manage permissions and ignore files.

Upstream integration points:
Config loading, legacy compatibility, environment overrides, setters,
saving, summaries, and reload fingerprints live in jcode-base. Gateway,
provider setup, TUI commands and pickers, and server runtime commands expose
save outcomes. Config edit watches track logical and canonical paths for
both files. AgentModelsChanged carries optional value-free notices with
backward-compatible defaults. Existing enforced configuration policies
continue to run after the merged input and environment layer. Dependency
1007 supplies the policy-gated loader and remote-command context extended
here; private overrides must preserve that enforced behavior.

Update guidance:
Preserve recursive table merging, whole-array replacement, logical-home
lookup, private-only loading, and safe private-file error diagnostics.
Use main-only update loading for explicit mutations, including values equal
to effective private overrides. Effective-load save deltas are defensive,
not an explicit mutation API. Preserve main symlinks, private bytes and
symlinks, unknown main settings, and value-free output. Warn only about
changed keys whose requested values remain privately overridden, including
structured keys and added or removed tables without sibling overreach.
Keep private reload identity, listeners, auth invalidation, truthful stored
versus session outcomes, protocol compatibility, and durable configuration
documentation in sync. Do not introduce dependencies on execution plans.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-base private_config --lib
cargo test -p jcode-base change_report --lib
cargo test -p jcode-base private_override_blocks_effect_but_main_change_is_saved --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core config_edit_notice --lib
cargo test -p jcode-app-core global_agent_model_request_updates_server_config_not_session --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui private_config --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui blocked_toggle_renders_notices_without_restart_claim --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui effective_toggle_keeps_restart_instructions --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui persisted_change_blocked_by_private_reports_not_effective --lib
cargo test -p jcode-protocol test_agent_models --lib
cargo test -p jcode provider_setup --lib
