diff --git a/docs/CONFIGURATION.md b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..af36f6aad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CONFIGURATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+# Configuration Files: main and private
+
+jcode reads settings from two TOML files in the jcode home directory
+(`~/.jcode` by default, or `$JCODE_HOME`):
+
+- `config.toml` — the main configuration file. This is the file jcode writes.
+- `config.private.toml` — an optional override file. jcode never writes to it.
+
+Both files are plain, user-readable TOML. Nothing in either file is encrypted
+or hidden from the user who owns the home directory.
+
+## Precedence
+
+Effective settings resolve in this order, later layers overriding earlier
+ones:
+
+1. Built-in defaults
+2. `config.toml` (main)
+3. `config.private.toml` (private override)
+4. Environment variables
+
+Environment variables still win over both files. The private file exists so a
+user can pin settings on a machine without those pins being copied into a
+dotfiles-managed or agent-written main config.
+
+## Merge semantics
+
+The private file is merged into the main document at load time:
+
+- Tables merge recursively: a private `[display]` table overrides only the
+  keys it sets and leaves other `display.*` keys to the main file.
+- Every other value replaces wholesale: scalars, arrays (including arrays of
+  tables) supplied by the private file replace the entire merged value at
+  that path, and a private table that lands where the main file has a
+  non-table value replaces that whole subtree.
+
+Key paths are structured: segments stay whole, so a dynamic name containing a
+dot (for example a provider id `my.gateway` in `[providers."my.gateway"]`) is
+one path segment and never aliases a differently nested key. Dotted *display*
+strings such as `providers.my.gateway.model` are ambiguous by nature; the
+override checks use the structured segments, not the display string.
+
+## Errors
+
+- A main file that fails to parse produces the regular parser error; it can
+  only quote the main file.
+- A private file that fails to parse produces a value-free error: the file
+  name, a line/column position, and at most a key name. Parser messages can
+  embed source excerpts, so they are never surfaced for the private file.
+- A config that fails to load makes jcode fall back to default settings, and
+  edits are followed by an explicit warning naming the file that no longer
+  parses (a valid edit to one file is never blamed for the other file's
+  syntax error).
+
+## Writes
+
+jcode only ever writes `config.toml`:
+
+- Saves are delta-based against the loaded baseline, so unknown or
+  hand-maintained main-file values survive a typed save.
+- Private values and environment values are never copied into the main file.
+- When a just-saved setting is shadowed by a conflicting private override,
+  jcode reports a value-free notice ("saved, but not effective") naming the
+  key and the private file. A private override equal to the requested value
+  is not a conflict and produces no warning.
+- Writes to the raw main file by tools such as `jcode provider add` compute
+  the same before/after notices, and UI surfaces (gateway toggles, cache TTL
+  saves, default-model saves, remote agent-model events) render these notices
+  instead of claiming success.
+
+## Symlinks
+
+- The main config path may be a symlink (for example into a dotfiles repo);
+  writes follow the symlink and the link itself is preserved.
+- The private file is always resolved beside the *logical* main config path
+  in the jcode home, never beside the symlink target, so private settings
+  stay local when the main config is shared across machines.
+
+## Warnings
+
+- Private-file edits are summarized with key paths and the file name only;
+  private values are never rendered in tool output, reports, or logs.
+- Debug output for save outcomes and load provenance is value-free by
+  construction.
+- Blocked changes and the file that supplies a setting are reported
+  separately: "supplied by config.private.toml" is a source label, while
+  "saved, but not effective" is a blocked outcome.
+
+## Example
+
+A private override file (`~/.jcode/config.private.toml`):
+
+```toml
+# Overrides the main config on this machine only.
+[display]
+centered = true
+
+[provider]
+default_model = "my-local-model"
+```
+
+This example is parsed by a test in `crates/jcode-base` to keep the
+documentation honest.
+
+## See also
+
+- `docs/AUTH_CREDENTIAL_SOURCES.md` for where credentials live and how the
+  files above interact with environment-based credentials.
+- `docs/TUI_COLOR_CONFIGURATION.md` for configuring colors in the same
+  two-file scheme.
